{
  "category": "Sleeping Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Very lazy. Just eats and sleeps. As its rotund bulk builds, it becomes steadily more slothful.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very lazy. Just eats and sleeps. As its rotund bulk builds, it becomes steadily more slothful.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Will eat anything, even if the food happens to be a little moldy. It never gets an upset stomach.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "What sounds like its cry may actually be its snores or the rumblings of its hungry belly.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its stomach's digestive juices can dissolve any kind of poison. It can even eat things off the ground.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON's stomach is so strong, even eating moldy or rotten food will not affect it.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "SNORLAX’s typical day consists of nothing more than eating and sleeping. It is such a docile POKéMON that there are children who use its expansive belly as a place to play.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "SNORLAX’s typical day consists of nothing more than eating and sleeping. It is such a docile POKéMON that there are children who use its expansive belly as a place to play.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "SNORLAX’s typical day consists of nothing more than eating and sleeping. It is such a docile POKéMON that there are children who use its big belly as a place to play.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is not satisfied unless it eats over 880 pounds of food every day. When it is done eating, it goes promptly to sleep.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very lazy. Just eats and sleeps. As its rotund bulk builds, it becomes steadily more slothful.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its stomach can digest any kind of food, even if it happens to be moldy or rotten.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It stops eating only to sleep. It doesn’t feel full unless it eats nearly 900 pounds a day.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its belly is full, it becomes too lethargic to even lift a finger, so it is safe to bounce on its belly.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
