      "text": "Its stomach can digest any kind of food, even if it happens to be moldy or rotten.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Snorlax’s typical day consists of nothing more than eating and sleeping. It is such a docile Pokémon that there are children who use its expansive belly as a place to play.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Snorlax’s typical day consists of nothing more than eating and sleeping. It is such a docile Pokémon that there are children who use its expansive belly as a place to play.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its stomach is said to be incomparably strong. Even Muk’s poison is nothing more than a hint of spice on Snorlax’s tongue.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It eats nearly 900 pounds of food every day. It starts nodding off while eating—and continues to eat even while it’s asleep.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It doesn’t do anything other than eat and sleep. When prompted to make a serious effort, though, it apparently displays awesome power.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has no interest in anything other than eating. Even if you climb up on its stomach while it’s napping, it doesn’t seem to mind at all!",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Will eat anything, even if the food happens to be a little moldy. It never gets an upset stomach.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Will eat anything, even if the food happens to be a little moldy. It never gets an upset stomach.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is not satisfied unless it eats over 880 pounds of food every day. When it is done eating, it goes promptly to sleep.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon’s stomach is so strong, even eating moldy or rotten food will not affect it.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "This glutton appears in villages without warning and devours the entirety of their rice granaries—such occurrences have long been counted among the gravest of disasters.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
